    "detailedAnswer": "Problem: Upper bound.\nSample input: [1,2,2,4],2\nExpected output: 3\n\nApproach: Find first value greater than target.\n\nJava solution:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nint upper(int[] a,int t){int l=0,r=a.length;while(l<r){int m=l+(r-l)/2;if(a[m]<=t)l=m+1;else r=m;}return l;}\n\nTime complexity: O(log n)\nSpace complexity: O(1)\nAssume valid inputs and values within numeric limits unless stated otherwise.",
    "detailedAnswerTelugu": "సమస్య: Upper bound\nఉదాహరణ input: [1,2,2,4],2\nExpected output: 3\n\nపరిష్కారం: target కంటే ఎక్కువైన మొదటి విలువను వెతకండి.\n\nJava code:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nint upper(int[] a,int t){int l=0,r=a.length;while(l<r){int m=l+(r-l)/2;if(a[m]<=t)l=m+1;else r=m;}return l;}\n\nTime complexity: O(log n)\nSpace complexity: O(1)\nసరైన input మరియు numeric limits లోని విలువలను ఉపయోగించండి.",
