    "detailedAnswer": "Problem: Stack using queue.\nSample input: push 1,2; pop\nExpected output: 2\n\nApproach: Rotate queue after insertion.\n\nJava solution:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nclass S{Queue<Integer>q=new ArrayDeque<>();void push(int x){q.add(x);for(int i=1;i<q.size();i++)q.add(q.remove());}int pop(){return q.remove();}}\n\nTime complexity: O(n) push\nSpace complexity: O(n)\nAssume valid inputs and values within numeric limits unless stated otherwise.",
