    "detailedAnswer": "Problem: Remove nth node from end.\nSample input: 1->2->3,2\nExpected output: 1->3\n\nApproach: Maintain n-node gap.\n\nJava solution:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Node: int val; Node next; Node(int val) constructor.\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nNode remove(Node h,int n){Node d=new Node(0);d.next=h;Node f=d,s=d;for(int i=0;i<n;i++)f=f.next;while(f.next!=null){f=f.next;s=s.next;}s.next=s.next.next;return d.next;}\n\nTime complexity: O(n)\nSpace complexity: O(1)\nAssume valid inputs and values within numeric limits unless stated otherwise.",
