    "question": "Coin change minimum",
    "shortAnswer": "Build minimum counts for smaller amounts",
    "detailedAnswer": "Problem: Coin change minimum.\nSample input: [1,2,5],11\nExpected output: 3\n\nApproach: Build minimum counts for smaller amounts.\n\nJava solution:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nint coins(int[] a,int t){int[] d=new int[t+1];Arrays.fill(d,t+1);d[0]=0;for(int i=1;i<=t;i++)for(int c:a)if(c<=i)d[i]=Math.min(d[i],1+d[i-c]);return d[t]>t?-1:d[t];}\n\nTime complexity: O(n t)\nSpace complexity: O(t)\nAssume valid inputs and values within numeric limits unless stated otherwise.",
    "detailedAnswerTelugu": "సమస్య: Coin change minimum\nఉదాహరణ input: [1,2,5],11\nExpected output: 3\n\nపరిష్కారం: చిన్న amounts కు కనిష్ఠ coins లెక్కించండి.\n\nJava code:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nint coins(int[] a,int t){int[] d=new int[t+1];Arrays.fill(d,t+1);d[0]=0;for(int i=1;i<=t;i++)for(int c:a)if(c<=i)d[i]=Math.min(d[i],1+d[i-c]);return d[t]>t?-1:d[t];}\n\nTime complexity: O(n t)\nSpace complexity: O(t)\nసరైన input మరియు numeric limits లోని విలువలను ఉపయోగించండి.",
