    "detailedAnswer": "Problem: Longest common subsequence.\nSample input: abc,ac\nExpected output: 2\n\nApproach: Match characters or skip one.\n\nJava solution:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nint lcs(String a,String b){int[][]d=new int[a.length()+1][b.length()+1];for(int i=1;i<=a.length();i++)for(int j=1;j<=b.length();j++)d[i][j]=a.charAt(i-1)==b.charAt(j-1)?1+d[i-1][j-1]:Math.max(d[i-1][j],d[i][j-1]);return d[a.length()][b.length()];}\n\nTime complexity: O(nm)\nSpace complexity: O(nm)\nAssume valid inputs and values within numeric limits unless stated otherwise.",
