    "shortAnswer": "Update capacities backwards to avoid reuse",
    "detailedAnswer": "Problem: Zero one knapsack.\nSample input: weights [1,3],values [2,5],capacity 3\nExpected output: 5\n\nApproach: Update capacities backwards to avoid reuse.\n\nJava solution:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nint bag(int[] w,int[] v,int c){int[]d=new int[c+1];for(int i=0;i<w.length;i++)for(int j=c;j>=w[i];j--)d[j]=Math.max(d[j],d[j-w[i]]+v[i]);return d[c];}\n\nTime complexity: O(nc)\nSpace complexity: O(c)\nAssume valid inputs and values within numeric limits unless stated otherwise.",
    "detailedAnswerTelugu": "సమస్య: Zero one knapsack\nఉదాహరణ input: weights [1,3],values [2,5],capacity 3\nExpected output: 5\n\nపరిష్కారం: ఒక item మళ్లీ వాడకుండా capacity వెనుక నుంచి update చేయండి.\n\nJava code:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nint bag(int[] w,int[] v,int c){int[]d=new int[c+1];for(int i=0;i<w.length;i++)for(int j=c;j>=w[i];j--)d[j]=Math.max(d[j],d[j-w[i]]+v[i]);return d[c];}\n\nTime complexity: O(nc)\nSpace complexity: O(c)\nసరైన input మరియు numeric limits లోని విలువలను ఉపయోగించండి.",
    "difficulty": "advanced",
