    "shortAnswer": "Sort starts and extend overlapping interval",
    "detailedAnswer": "Problem: Merge overlapping intervals.\nSample input: [[1,3],[2,6],[8,9]]\nExpected output: [[1,6],[8,9]]\n\nApproach: Sort starts and extend overlapping interval.\n\nJava solution:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nList<int[]> merge(int[][]a){Arrays.sort(a,Comparator.comparingInt(x->x[0]));List<int[]>r=new ArrayList<>();for(int[] x:a){if(r.isEmpty()||r.getLast()[1]<x[0])r.add(x.clone());else r.getLast()[1]=Math.max(r.getLast()[1],x[1]);}return r;}\n\nTime complexity: O(n log n)\nSpace complexity: O(n)\nAssume valid inputs and values within numeric limits unless stated otherwise.",
    "detailedAnswerTelugu": "సమస్య: Merge overlapping intervals\nఉదాహరణ input: [[1,3],[2,6],[8,9]]\nExpected output: [[1,6],[8,9]]\n\nపరిష్కారం: start ప్రకారం sort చేసి overlap interval ను పొడిగించండి.\n\nJava code:\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n// Method or class excerpt; place methods inside a Java class.\nList<int[]> merge(int[][]a){Arrays.sort(a,Comparator.comparingInt(x->x[0]));List<int[]>r=new ArrayList<>();for(int[] x:a){if(r.isEmpty()||r.getLast()[1]<x[0])r.add(x.clone());else r.getLast()[1]=Math.max(r.getLast()[1],x[1]);}return r;}\n\nTime complexity: O(n log n)\nSpace complexity: O(n)\nసరైన input మరియు numeric limits లోని విలువలను ఉపయోగించండి.",
